    {
      "designator": "CS23-0",
      "grouping_at_time": "Subpart D \u2014 Design And Construction",
      "title_at_revision": "Hulls",
      "text": "(a) The hull of a hull seaplane or amphibian of 680 kg (1 500 lb) or more maximum weight must have watertight compartments designed and arranged so that the hull, auxiliary floats and tyres (if used), will keep the aeroplane afloat without capsizing in fresh water when \u2013\n  (1) For aeroplanes of 2 268 kg (5 000 lb) or more maximum weight, any two adjacent compartments are flooded; and\n  (2) For aeroplanes of 680 kg (1 500 lb) up to, but not including 2 268 kg (5 000 lb) maximum weight, any single compartment is flooded.\n(b) Watertight doors in bulkheads may be used for communication between compartments.",
      "publication_cite": "ED Decision 2003/014/RM",
